# Copy this file to .env and fill in before building/deploying the frontend.
# NEVER commit the real .env file.

# ── REQUIRED for a deployed build ───────────────────────────────────────
# The URL of your deployed backend (e.g. https://jaldrishti-backend.onrender.com).
# Do NOT include a trailing slash.
#
# If left blank, the app falls back to http://localhost:4000 — correct for
# local development, but WRONG once deployed: the deployed frontend would
# try to reach the visitor's own machine, not your real backend, and every
# API call (login, Earth Engine, etc.) would silently fail.
#
# This must be set at BUILD time (Vite bakes it into the static bundle) —
# setting it only in your hosting platform's runtime environment does
# nothing for a static site. Set it as a build-time environment variable
# in your hosting platform's dashboard before running `npm run build`.
VITE_API_URL=